  "table_version": 1,
  "_doc": [
    "Relative-date phrase table. DATA, NOT CODE (TR-EXT-052): adding a locale is",
    "an edit to this file and nothing else. T-073's acceptance is exactly that.",
    "",
    "Matching is deliberately order-agnostic. The resolver looks for a quantity",
    "and a unit anywhere in the phrase, which handles suffix ordering ('2 weeks",
    "ago'), prefix ordering ('vor 2 Wochen'), and multi-word prefixes ('il y a 2",
    "semaines') with one mechanism instead of three.",
    "",
    "'articles' are the words a locale uses to mean exactly one. TRD 21.6.1's",
    "Agent Note names their absence as the parser bug that passes a naive test",
    "suite and then fails on every 'a day ago' and 'yesterday' in the corpus -",
    "which are the most common phrasings on recent reviews, and therefore the",
    "ones a 'newest first' display shows most prominently.",
    "",
    "'special' phrases carry their own quantity and unit because they name a",
    "duration without stating a number."
  ],
